# Check2GO Android

- Android is Kotlin + Jetpack Compose.
- Do not modify `app/ios/` for Android tasks.
- Historical Flutter/APK material is reference only.
- Read `docs/source-priority.md`, `docs/platform-parity.md`, `docs/design/design-tokens.md`, and `docs/android/architecture.md` before architectural changes.
- Preserve package/application id `co.check2go` unless explicitly approved.
- Keep business rules outside composables.
- Prefer immutable UI state and Android-native state holders.
- Do not invent missing Figma values. Mark temporary UI clearly when exact values are unknown.
- Do not connect historical AWS environments or add credentials without explicit approval.
- Never commit secrets, API keys, tokens, `.env`, keystores, signing files, or production user data.
- Use an `android/<task>` branch and open a PR; do not develop directly on `main`.
